e6d","body":"Claimed; beginning held-out TDD in worktree scanner-promote.","timestamp":1788639187111770001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"RED/GREEN evidence: RED targeted tests failed for missing scanner-integration in vote.needs, missing gerrit-verify job, missing normalize route checks, scanner still in EXCLUDED_JOBS, and missing predates closure. GREEN targeted pytest passed: 105 passed. Mutation: sandboxed removal of scanner job/vote references killed the oracle (4 expected failures). Local gates: check_verify_gate_parity OK; make lint OK; make typecheck OK; scanner lock validation OK; full make scanner-integration unsupported on macOS darwin/arm64 (linux-only lane), will be proven by Gerrit GHA.","timestamp":1788639612939048001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"STOPPED per anti-90c7 guardrail: Gerrit change 2682 was pushed for review, but its own Verified workflow run https://github.com/navapbc/rebar/actions/runs/33989904007 did not include a scanner-integration job in the Gerrit Verified Gate job list. A separate gerrit-scanner advisory workflow did run, but scanner-integration was not part of this change's required Verified aggregate because workflow_dispatch used trusted main's gerrit-verify.yaml. Marked CL 2682 WIP; not submitting. Blocker: co-locating the new job in gerrit-verify.yaml cannot prove non-vacuous execution on the introducing change without an already-landed aggregation mechanism or another safe rollout path.","timestamp":1788640814978443001}],"created_at":1788636785013208001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"605f1126-bfb5-4ba1-9a57-9528b97c31e5","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"283b-7104-87c1-4015"},{"link_uuid":"2b9dae47-24c2-4059-90cc-8cea846709fa","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"53fc-fc82-d779-4e68"}],"description":"## Context\n- Epic 78f2-b104-e3c9-4b86 requires promoting review `scanner-integration` from advisory to voting within the Gerrit `Verified` aggregate.\n- Incident 90c7 showed two failure classes to avoid: a vacuous Verified vote where a newly-required job did not run on its own introducing change, followed by a portability defect that made the lane red for every downstream change.\n- Promotion is safe now because the advisory lane is landed and validated green on real GHA (story aa9e-3d35-fd3e-41ee, CL 2666, merge SHA 4c9940348148fb255b17ddf1cb124701ad4565d7, run https://github.com/navapbc/rebar/actions/runs/33985796177), and b973-b298-9b5d-4765 closed the vacuous-vote escape with a predates-gate guard and lane-derived parity coverage.\n\n## Scope\n- Add a concrete `scanner-integration` job inside `.github/workflows/gerrit-verify.yaml`, gated to the full route with the same `if:` shape as build-and-test/optionality, calling `./.github/workflows/_scanner-integration.yml` with the Gerrit refspec/project/url so it actually runs on the patchset.\n- Add `scanner-integration` to `.github/workflows/gerrit-verify.yaml` voting needs, vote normalization, and required workflow-conclusion aggregation so scanner failure blocks Verified.\n- Reverse ADR-0114 advisory state in `scripts/check_verify_gate_parity.py` and `docs/adr/0114-advisory-gate-before-hot-path.md`, so mirror-vs-Verified parity requires scanner-integration in the voting aggregate.\n- Keep real mirror surfaces coherent: `.github/workflows/test.yml`, `.github/workflows/gerrit-scanner-verify.yml`, and reusable `_scanner-integration.yml`. Jenkinsfile is a negative-control inspection only: it is reconcile-bridge-only and will not be edited for this scanner gate unless investigation proves otherwise, in which case this ticket stops for scope revision.\n- Update direct string/symbol coverage inventory: `tests/unit/test_code_review_ws5.py`, `tests/unit/test_verify_gate_parity.py`, `tests/unit/test_gerrit_verify_triage_comment.py`, `tests/unit/test_workflow_names.py`, `tests/unit/test_ci_workflow_parity.py`, and `tests/unit/test_predates_gate_guard_parity.py`.\n\n## Anti-90c7 safety design\n- Non-vacuous proof: add `scanner-integration` coverage to `tests/unit/test_predates_gate_guard_parity.py` and the lane-derived parity tests, then before submit record the promoting change's own Gerrit Verified run URL/job showing `scanner-integration` executed and passed (not skipped).\n- Back-out: if the promoted lane goes red on main, revert this CL to restore the ADR-0114 advisory exception and remove scanner-integration from voting needs, immediately unblocking downstream Verified.\n- Portability and route safety: do not introduce bash-only shell options or a GitHub-only mechanism. Preserve POSIX-dash-safe Make recipes and mirrored GHA workflow semantics under parity tests. Thread scanner-integration through BOTH route arms: full route requires `needs.scanner-integration.result == 'success'`; docs-only route requires `needs.scanner-integration.result == 'skipped'`, preventing prose-only changes from failing because the full-route scanner did not run.\n\n## Testing\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" pytest tests/unit/test_gerrit_verify_triage_comment.py tests/unit/test_workflow_names.py tests/unit/test_ci_workflow_parity.py tests/unit/test_predates_gate_guard_parity.py tests/unit/test_code_review_ws5.py tests/unit/test_verify_gate_parity.py` proves vote routing, both normalize route arms, workflow naming, parity, newly-added scanner predates coverage, and reversed advisory assertions.\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" python scripts/check_verify_gate_parity.py` proves scanner-integration is required by voting parity.\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make lint` proves formatting, ruff, module-size, complexity, mechanism-delta, and workflow parity gates.\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make typecheck` proves static typing remains green.\n- Sandboxed mutation removes `scanner-integration` from the voting aggregate and confirms the held-out parity/predates oracle fails, then restores.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `pytest tests/unit/test_ci_workflow_parity.py` proves a `scanner-integration` job exists inside `gerrit-verify.yaml`, calls `_scanner-integration.yml` with Gerrit patchset inputs, and executes automatically on the full Gerrit Verified route rather than only by manual dispatch.\n- [ ] `pytest tests/unit/test_gerrit_verify_triage_comment.py` proves `gerrit-verify.yaml` includes `scanner-integration` in voting needs, full-route success normalization, docs-only skipped normalization, and required workflow-conclusion aggregation; a scanner failure blocks Verified.\n- [ ] `python scripts/check_verify_gate_parity.py` and `pytest tests/unit/test_verify_gate_parity.py` pass only when `scanner-integration` is required in the voting aggregate and removed from ADR-0114 advisory exceptions.\n- [ ] Newly-added assertions in `pytest tests/unit/test_predates_gate_guard_parity.py` prove predates-gate/parity coverage includes `scanner-integration` and prevents a vacuous vote where the new job did not execute on its own introducing change.\n- [ ] `pytest tests/unit/test_workflow_names.py tests/unit/test_code_review_ws5.py tests/unit/test_ci_workflow_parity.py` proves GHA/mirror scanner workflow coherence, advisory assertion reversal, and POSIX portability without relying on Jenkinsfile.\n- [ ] `make lint && make typecheck` plus targeted pytest above pass locally with `.venv/bin` first on PATH.\n- [ ] [non-codebase] Gerrit evidence recorded in a ticket comment includes change id, `LLM-Review +1`, `Verified +1`, run URL/job id, timestamp, and a non-skipped `scanner-integration` job that passed on this promoting change before submit.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":".github/workflows/gerrit-verify.yaml","reason":"Promote scanner-integration into Gerrit Verified voting aggregate and automatic patchset execution."},{"path":".github/workflows/_scanner-integration.yml","reason":"Keep reusable scanner lane callable and coherent when required by Verified."},{"path":".github/workflows/gerrit-scanner-verify.yml","reason":"Update former advisory scanner workflow semantics affected by promotion."},{"path":".github/workflows/test.yml","reason":"Maintain mirror workflow parity for required scanner-integration coverage."},{"path":"scripts/check_verify_gate_parity.py","reason":"Remove ADR-0114 advisory exception and require scanner-integration parity."},{"path":"docs/adr/0114-advisory-gate-before-hot-path.md","reason":"Update ADR text so scanner-integration is no longer documented as advisory."},{"path":"tests/unit/test_code_review_ws5.py","reason":"Reverse hard-coded advisory scanner workflow invariant."},{"path":"tests/unit/test_verify_gate_parity.py","reason":"Cover check_verify_gate_parity behavior without scanner-integration exclusion."},{"path":"tests/unit/test_gerrit_verify_triage_comment.py","reason":"Cover vote.needs route and triage normalization for scanner-integration as voting."},{"path":"tests/unit/test_workflow_names.py","reason":"Update workflow naming expectations after scanner lane promotion."},{"path":"tests/unit/test_ci_workflow_parity.py","reason":"Assert mirror-vs-Verified scanner parity and POSIX portability."},{"path":"tests/unit/test_predates_gate_guard_parity.py","reason":"Prove predates-gate guard covers scanner-integration so the vote is non-vacuous."},{"path":".github/mechanism-baseline.json","reason":"Update mechanism baseline only if the required promotion creates justified mechanism-delta changes."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["depends_on","283b-7104-87c1-4015"],["parent","78f2-b104-e3c9-4b86"],["relates_to","53fc-fc82-d779-4e68"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"78f2-b104-e3c9-4b86","parent_status_uuid":"0a248ae4-4e82-4f84-99b5-b1bbeb9fe4e7","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"st